WEBVTT

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:06.677
One character. Many scenes. Every detail under control.

00:00:07.100 --> 00:00:13.415
A local Flux Three studio. One original character, in three new scenes.

00:00:14.100 --> 00:00:17.755
Create an original design from your description.

00:00:21.100 --> 00:00:26.772
Keep the original reference as your identity anchor. Create a new setting.

00:00:29.100 --> 00:00:35.607
The official local upsampler reads your request and reference. Both descriptions are saved.

00:00:37.100 --> 00:00:44.687
Paint one detail. Nearby context guides the edit. A keyboard rectangle works too.

00:00:45.100 --> 00:00:49.825
Generation runs locally. Waiting is shortened here.

00:00:50.300 --> 00:00:55.727
The bag is teal. Original dimensions are preserved.

00:00:57.300 --> 00:01:03.320
Compare the result with its source. Details inside your selection may also change.

00:01:07.300 --> 00:01:11.879
Four tested edits changed zero pixels outside their effective feathered masks.

00:01:14.300 --> 00:01:27.013
Export the input, mask, result, observed prompt and actual workflow together.

00:01:27.500 --> 00:01:35.569
Our contribution: recoverable jobs, persistent history, precise local edits, and reproducible recipes.

00:01:37.500 --> 00:01:47.618
Thirteen jobs completed. Six recognizable reference identities. One walking pose failed. We kept that case.

00:01:48.100 --> 00:01:57.115
Run the studio locally. Find the source, setup, model licenses and measured limits on GitHub.
